# Component / service IO boundary

- Components **must not perform IO directly**. HTTP, persistence, storage, external APIs, and other external-resource access belong to an owning registered service consumed through `$svc(...)`.
- Components express application intent through semantic operations such as `$svc('orders').submit(order)`.
- Endpoint paths, HTTP methods, transport payload names, protocol conventions, and technical response normalization belong to the owning service.
- Domain services may use lower-level primitives such as `$svc('ajax')`; do not expose a generic `post(path, payload)` wrapper as an application API.
- Services own coherent non-visual application capabilities, including central behavior that has only one current caller when the knowledge belongs to the capability.
- Components remain responsible for rendering, DOM interaction, focus, modals, visual notifications, routing UI, and local UI state.
- Do not move deterministic domain calculations into a client service when another layer is already their source of truth.

Details and examples: `ai-instructions/services.md`.
